  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reintegration Assistance from Belgium 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Reintegration Assistance Project complements the Assisted Voluntary Return (AVR) programme in Belgium. The project contributes to the sustainable reintegration of beneficiaries in their Countries of Origin (CoOs), considering their vulnerabilities. In the implementation, IOM works closely with IOM missions worldwide, and cooperates with a variety of partners in Belgium and in CoOs. Reintegration assistance is provided in-kind. Reintegration support ranges from income-generating activities, material support, housing assistance, as well as trainings and educational activities, to medical and psycho-social assistance. The specific vulnerabilities of each beneficiary are identified through a gender-sensitive needs assessment during the pre-departure counselling and through active liaison with the referring AVR partners in Belgium and IOM Missions in CoOs.</narrative>
  </description>
